    description: "ADR-0057 §5 sets the built-in arbitration default to incumbent-first \"until a\nper-attribute measurement shows otherwise\", and §10 lets a backend declare\n`authoritative_for` only with a cited measurement. TODAY THAT MEASUREMENT IS\nA SCRATCHPAD SCRIPT. Nothing in the repo produces it, so the default can\nnever legitimately change and adding a higher-fidelity backend changes no\ncontested attribute. LIVE.md rule 7: an instrument with no reader is the same\norganic criterion in a costume.\n\nWHAT IT PRODUCES, given one artifact containing >=2 producers for a language\n(or two single-producer artifacts of the same tree):\n  1. Pairing table: paired / only-A / only-B counts by kind, using each\n     backend's declared merge anchor (the contract row), so the tool and the\n     pass agree on what \"the same declaration\" means.\n  2. Per-attribute agreement table: for every attribute both producers set,\n     agree / disagree counts with up to N examples of each disagreement\n     shape (e.g. kind: method vs function, 52 of 52 free functions).\n  3. Edge-overlap table: per edge_type, in-repo vs external target, edges\n     seen by A only / B only / both, on paired endpoints.\n  4. Output formatted as a docs/audits/ verdict table (docs/audits/README.md\n     format) so it can be committed and CITED by an authority declaration.\n\nFIRST EXPECTED OUTPUT (aardvark-dns, b1008d3b67, HYPERGUMBO_RUST_ANALYZER=1;\nthis is the reference the tool must reproduce): 138/169 SCIP paired, 0\ntree-sitter leftovers, 31 SCIP-only (18 namespace, 11 variable, 2 class);\ncallable->callable edges SCIP 99 / tree-sitter 100 / both 92; all outgoing\n287 / 376 / 98; SCIP-only targets 79 field, 49 variable, 51 type; tree-sitter\nonly 268 external_symbol; SCIP external edges 0; kind disagrees 52/52 on\nfree functions.\n\nRULE THIS ROW INSTALLS: no built-in default exception and no\n`authoritative_for` entry may be added except by citing a committed table\nproduced by this tool. Put that sentence in the ADR-0057 §5 text on landing.\n\nPREREQUISITE: the cache-key row — a stale artifact from the other backend\nset silently corrupts every number above.\n\nSubcommand vs script is the implementing PR's call; a subcommand is\npreferred so the measurement runs on the same artifact the user has."  # 244a
    fields: {}  # 244a
